This version dereferences `mDefinition` once into a local reference and uses a single conditional expression. Behaviour is unchanged: the same calls run in the same order with the same results. The only saving is avoiding repeated smart-pointer dereferences, so expect any speedup to be very small.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 DeveloperField::GetType() const
{
    const auto& def = *mDefinition;
    return def.IsDefined() ? static_cast<FIT_UINT8>(def.GetType())
                           : static_cast<FIT_UINT8>(FIT_BASE_TYPE_UINT8);
}
```